    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\r\n\r\nOlder version of nvim correctly detects latest version of Neovim::Ext as 0.06 when using :checkhealth\r\n\r\nCurrent dev version improperly reports current version incorrectly as 5 and with 0.06 installed being out of date as below:\r\n\r\n- WARNING Module \"Neovim::Ext\" is out-of-date. Installed: 0.06, latest: 5\r\n  - ADVICE:\r\n    - Run in shell: cpanm -n Neovim::Ext\r\n\r\nFrom what I can tell, the command to get the string to regex and get current version evaluates to the following on my local machine:\r\n\r\n    /usr/bin/perl -MApp::cpanminus::script -e 'my $app = App::cpanminus::script->new; $app->parse_options (\"--info\", \"-q\", \"Neovim::Ext\"); exit $app->doit'\r\n\r\nwhich when run from command line gives an error containing `Can't locate App/cpanminus/script.pm in @INC (you may need to install the App::cpanminus::script`\r\n\r\n`cpan -i App::cpanminus::script` fails on the local machine as follows:\r\n\r\n    (error): Could not expand [App::cpanminus::script]. Check the module name.\r\n    (info): I can suggest names if you install one of Text::Levenshtein::XS, Text::Levenshtein::Damerau::XS, Text::Levenshtein, and Text::Levenshtein::Damerau::PP\r\n    (info): and you provide the -x option on invocation.\r\n    (error): Skipping App::cpanminus::script because I couldn't find a matching namespace.\r\n\r\n\r\nPerhaps this is a local perl configuration error, but I wanted to post as a possible bug report as the old way of checking for current Neovim::Ext in nvim 0.6.1 behaves as intended.\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n1. Install nvim from latest repo\r\n2. run :checkhealth from within nvim\r\n3. see that incorrect newest version of Neovim::Ext is 5 instead of 0.06\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nExpected behavior would be for current dev version to report that Neovim::Ext 0.06 is installed and is up to date\r\n\r\n### Neovim version (nvim -v)\r\n\r\nv0.10.0-dev\r\n\r\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\r\n\r\nunknown\r\n\r\n### Operating system/version\r\n\r\nLinux Mint 21.1\r\n\r\n### Terminal name/version\r\n\r\nxterm-256color\r\n\r\n### $TERM environment variable\r\n\r\nscreen.xterm-256color\r\n\r\n### Installation\r\n\r\nbuilt from repo",
    "closed_at": null,
