            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> `/usr/bin/perl -MApp::cpanminus::script -e 'my $app = App::cpanminus::script->new; $app->parse_options (\"--info\", \"-q\", \"Neovim::Ext\"); exit $app->doit'`\r\n> \r\n> which when run from command line gives an error containing \"Can't locate App/cpanminus/script.pm in @inc (you may need to install the App::cpanminus::script\"\r\n> \r\n> cpan -i App::cpanminus::script fails ...\r\n> \r\n> Perhaps this is a local perl configuration error,\r\n\r\nSo... how can we check for the latest version? We need perl people to submit a fix for this. \r\n\r\nIf the perl provider doesn't get an owner we may end up removing it.",
