            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Since it's been a few years since this was last looked at, I thought I'd recheck things.\n\n```\n$ perl '-MApp::cpanminus::script' -e 'my $app = App::cpanminus::script->new; $app->parse_options (\"--info\", \"-q\", \"Neovim::Ext\"); exit $app->doit'\nJACQUESG/Neovim-Ext-0.06.tar.gz\n```\n\nBut current neovim is instead looking for App::cpanminus::fatscript, which fails (as below) because cpanminus hasn't shipped fatscript.pm since 2018. (Commit c848b2e4044e3d78ef92f9eba0da168140c6aaeb if you're curious.)\n\n```\n$ perl '-MApp::cpanminus::fatscript' -e 'my $app = App::cpanminus::script->new; $app->parse_options (\"--info\", \"-q\", \"Neovim::Ext\"); exit $app->doit'\nCan't locate App/cpanminus/fatscript.pm in @INC (you may need to install the App::cpanminus::fatscript module) (@INC entries checked: /home/warp/perl5/lib/perl5/5.42.3/x86_64-linux-gnu-thread-multi /home/warp/perl5/lib/perl5/5.42.3 /home/warp/perl5/lib/perl5/x86_64-linux-gnu-thread-multi /home/warp/perl5/lib/perl5 /etc/perl /usr/local/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/perl/5.42.3 /usr/local/share/perl/5.42.3 /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/perl5/5.42 /usr/share/perl5 /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/perl-base /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/perl/5.42 /usr/share/perl/5.42 /home/warp/perl5/lib/perl5/5.42.2 /home/warp/perl5/lib/perl5/5.42.2/x86_64-linux-gnu-thread-multi /usr/local/lib/site_perl).\nBEGIN failed--compilation aborted.\n```\n\nCan we get a change with cpanminus::fatscript replaced with cpanminus::script? :)",
