            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "The problem is not cpanminus itself.\nThere are 4 failing test in the perl module. I cannot evaluate if they can be ignored or if they are critial. (perl module install workflow: fetch, test, make install)\n\nIt's not a good suggestion, but you can install it without running the tests before.\n```bash\ncpan  #start cpanshell\ncpan> notest install Neovim::Ext \n```\nSeems that the author of this module is still active, but the Neovim::Ext module was last updated in 2023...\n\nInstall without running the tests looks good in checkhealth:\n\n```vim\nvim.provider:                                                               ✅\n\nClipboard (optional) ~\n- ✅ OK Clipboard tool found: wl-copy\n\nNode.js provider (optional) ~\n- Disabled (loaded_node_provider=0).\n\nPerl provider (optional) ~\n- perl executable: /opt/sw/perl-5.42.2/bin/perl\n\nPython 3 provider (optional) ~\n- Disabled (loaded_python3_provider=0).\n\nRuby provider (optional) ~\n- Disabled (loaded_ruby_provider=0).\n\n```",
